{:id "0042-lab-synth"
 :title "Lab synth: a text synthesizer that plays patches (curves, oscillators, stagger), safe by construction"
 :lupa/deps #{"0041-lab-stage-flash-test"}
 :lupa/area :lab
 :lupa/risk :medium
 ;; Respecced 2026-11-17 after two reviews said REWORK, both for flaws in
 ;; the foreman's design: (1) the bounds check sampled two positions and
 ;; three ids, which is not sound (a slow :index wave on :blur passes and
 ;; then goes negative for half the letters); (2) :spring was pinned to 1
 ;; at the end but is 0.9917 just before it, so a spring that runs to the
 ;; end of a patch snaps on the last frame while the check said 'at rest'.
 ;; The design below fixes both; the reviewer's required changes are
 ;; acceptance criteria.
 :goal "docs/product/score.md: every gesture is a patch, data that moves a
        letter's channels along curves, optionally multiplied by an
        oscillator, staggered across the letters of a cue. Build the pure
        engine that plays a :ha/patch and the check that makes patches safe
        to accept from any agent: a patch with no problems ends at rest
        and never leaves its channels' bounds."
 :scope ["src/halfahead/lab/synth.cljc" "test/halfahead/lab/synth_test.cljc"]
 :design "Schema (the foreman's; do not edit): :ha/channel :ha/curve
          :ha/osc :ha/mod :ha/patch in src/halfahead/schema.cljc, with the
          meanings in its comments.
          halfahead.lab.synth (.cljc, pure, the same on both hosts):
          (curve k p) -> the value of :ha/curve k at p, p clamped to [0 1]:
            :one 1; :rise smoothstep p^2(3-2p); :fall 1 - smoothstep;
            :fade 1-p; :fade2 (1-p)^2; :arch sin(pi p); :arc 4p(1-p);
            :rise-sine sin(pi p / 2);
            :spring 1 - r(p), a damped spring's step response whose
              residual is faded out so that it lands exactly: r(p) =
              e^(-4.6 p) (cos(wd p) + (zeta / sqrt(1 - zeta^2)) sin(wd
              p)) with zeta 0.517 and wd = (4.6 / zeta) sqrt(1 - zeta^2)
              (the spring lab.pose uses for births; restate it), times
              (1 - smoothstep((p - 0.8) / 0.2)) for p > 0.8. So the curve
              is continuous on [0 1], overshoots as before, and its limit
              from below at 1 is exactly 1: nothing snaps;
            :spring-fall r(p) with the same fade: 1 at 0, exactly 0 at 1.
          (phase id salt) -> the fixed angle lab.pose's private phase
            gives: h = ((id mod 65521) * 7919 + salt * 104729) mod 65521,
            2 pi h / 65521. Restated here, with a test that pins three
            values.
          (start-ms patch pos n) -> when the letter at position pos (0
            based) of an n-letter cue starts: rank * step, step =
            :ms-per-glyph, compressed to max-ms / (n - 1) when the last
            letter would start after :max-ms (default 900; n <= 1 gives 0);
            rank is pos for :forward (the default), n - 1 - pos for
            :reverse, and the distance from the middle for :centre-out
            (the middle letter or pair starts first; there the step is
            compressed to max-ms / the largest rank, so the last letter
            to start does so within :max-ms). No :stagger: 0.
          (total-ms patch n) -> :ms plus the latest start.
          (delta patch u pos n id k) -> {channel delta} for that letter u
            ms after ITS OWN start, at intensity k: {} when u < 0 or u >=
            :ms. Otherwise, for every mod whose window [from to) of the
            patch's time contains u / ms (defaults 0 and 1), whose :each
            admits pos, add amount * k * sign * curve(q) * osc to its
            channel, q being the progress through the window, sign -1 on
            odd pos when :alternate?, and osc (when present) the wave at t
            = ms elapsed since the window's start: sin or cos of 2 pi t /
            period + phi, a triangle of the same period and phase (1 at
            phase 0), or :noise (deterministic value noise in [-1 1]: a
            hash of the step number floor(t / period), id and salt, each
            step eased into the next; the same on both hosts, small
            integers only); phi is 0 for :same (the default), pos * pi / 2
            for :index, (phase id salt) for :id (salt default 0); :abs?
            takes the absolute value. Mods on one channel add.
          bounds -> a public map channel -> [lo hi], the delta a patch may
            reach at intensity 1: :x [-0.5 0.5], :y [-2 2], :z [-3 3],
            :rx :ry :rz [-6.3 6.3], :scale :sx :sy [-0.9 3], :skew [-1 1],
            :weight [-1 1], :blur [0 1], :opacity [-0.95 0], :glow [0 1],
            :wobble [0 1], :tint [-1 1], :fill [-1 0].
          (problems patch) -> [] for a patch safe to play, else a vector
            of {:problem keyword ...} maps, in a stable order:
            :invalid (not a :ha/patch, with the humanized explanation, and
            nothing else is checked); :not-at-rest for each channel whose
            delta as u approaches :ms from below is not within 1e-6 of 0;
            :out-of-bounds for each channel that can leave bounds at any
            whole ms in [0 ms), with the worst :value. The check must be
            SOUND FOR EVERY LETTER, not a sample: positions 0 to 3 cover
            every quarter turn of :index, both parities and :alternate?;
            a mod whose oscillator has :phase :id or :wave :noise cannot
            be sampled, so it is bounded by its envelope (the oscillator
            taken as the interval [-1 1], or [0 1] with :abs?), and
            channels are summed as intervals. The rest check uses the
            limit from below (never a value pinned at the end). So a
            patch may be refused although no real letter would leave
            bounds (two :id-phase mods that would cancel): that is the
            price of soundness, and :value is then a bound, not a value
            some letter takes; say so in the docstring. Never throws,
            for any input at all.
          Tests: each curve's values at 0, 0.5 and 1 and its range on a
          grid, and that :spring and :spring-fall are continuous up to 1
          (the value at 1 - 1e-9 is within 1e-6 of the value at 1);
          start-ms for the three orders, compression and n of 0, 1 and 2;
          delta for a hand-made patch of each feature (windows, :each,
          :alternate?, each wave, each phase rule), including that a
          window's oscillator time starts at the window; problems for a
          patch that is fine, one invalid, one left displaced (:one on :y),
          one too far sideways (:x 0.8 :arch), a :spring that runs to the
          end (:not-at-rest, it ends on 1), and a :spring-fall that runs
          to the end (fine). Properties over generated valid patches. The
          generator must be honest: amounts that straddle the bounds,
          signed oscillators and :alternate? on one-sided channels, every
          curve in every window, positions up to 30, so that problems is
          what separates safe from unsafe; a test asserts the generator
          reaches both classes. delta is finite everywhere and {} outside
          [0 ms); deterministic; whenever (problems p) is [] the patch is
          within bounds (tolerance 1e-3 for what lies between whole ms)
          for random ids, positions 0 to 30 and times including
          fractions of a ms, and within 1e-6 of rest at ms - 1e-9;
          problems never throws on arbitrary data (gen/any)."
 :acceptance
 ["synth tests as in the design, on both hosts"
  "Regression tests, each asserting an :out-of-bounds problem: {:ms 400
   :mods [{:channel :blur :amount 0.8 :curve :arch :osc {:wave :sine
   :period-ms 1600 :phase :index}}]}; {:ms 50 :mods [{:channel :x :amount
   0.6 :curve :arch :osc {:wave :sine :period-ms 5000 :phase :id}}]};
   {:ms 400 :mods [{:channel :y :amount 2.6 :curve :arch :osc {:wave
   :noise :period-ms 400}}]}"
  "This patch (the foreman's :slam) has no problems: {:ms 900 :stagger
   {:ms-per-glyph 15 :max-ms 60} :mods [{:channel :scale :amount 1.4
   :curve :spring-fall} {:channel :z :amount 2.0 :curve :spring-fall}
   {:channel :weight :amount 0.8 :curve :fade2} {:channel :glow :amount
   0.7 :curve :fade2}]}"
  "The noise function's docstring says what is actually reduced before
   multiplying"
  "The patch in docs/product/score.md (:swell) has no problems, and its :y
   delta for position 0 at intensity 1 peaks at 0.2 at 900 ms"
  "`bb test` stays green"]
 :non-goals
 ["Do not touch lab.pose or any other namespace: wiring patches into the
   lab is the next order"
  "No gestures library here; do not edit the schema"
  "Do not run `bb e2e`, `bb play` or `bb lab:e2e`"]
 :context ["docs/product/score.md" "src/halfahead/schema.cljc"
           "src/halfahead/lab/pose.cljc" "DESIGN.md"]
 :budget-usd 10.0}
